      "path": "README.md",
      "content": "# Pixel Morse Code Translator\n\nAn offline browser app that translates text to Morse code and Morse code back to text.\n\n## Features\n\n- Type text and instantly see it in Morse code (letters separated by spaces, words by slashes).\n- Type Morse code and instantly see the decoded text.\n- Clear all fields with one button.\n- Fully keyboard accessible with labeled controls.\n- Responsive layout that works from 360px wide.\n- No external dependencies, network requests, or server code.\n\n## Usage\n\n1. Open `index.html` in any modern browser.\n2. In the **Text** box, type your message. The Morse code appears in the **Morse code** box below.\n3. In the **Morse code** box, type Morse code using spaces between letters and `/` between words. The decoded text appears in the **Decoded text** box below.\n4. Use the **Clear all** button to reset both translators.\n\n## Supported Characters\n\nLetters A–Z, digits 0–9, and common punctuation: `. , ? ' ! / ( ) & : ; = + - _ \" $ @`.\n\nUnsupported characters are ignored.\n\n## File Structure\n\n- `index.html` – markup and structure\n- `styles.css` – styling and responsive layout\n- `script.js` – translation logic and event handling\n- `README.md` – this file\n\n## License\n\nMIT",
